Mojtaba hooks list,
You can any other takeaways to the end of this list , however these are the most High Potential hooks.
Using These Syscalls must be practical , in theiory we can abused them but in practical security field it depends to different situations and conditions.


Process & Execution Hooks (High-Value)

    lsm/execve → Critical, attackers abuse it to hijack execution.

    lsm/bprm_check_security → Checks binaries before execution.

    lsm/task_create

    lsm/task_fix_setuid

    lsm/task_kill → Can deny signals (protect processes).

    lsm/task_getpgid

    lsm/task_getsid

Filesystem Hooks (Persistence & Data Access)

    lsm/inode_create

    lsm/inode_unlink

    lsm/inode_mkdir

    lsm/inode_symlink

    lsm/inode_permission → Super important for access control.

    lsm/inode_setattr

    lsm/inode_rename

File Operations Hooks

    lsm/file_open → Direct file open check.

    lsm/file_permission

    lsm/file_ioctl

    lsm/file_mprotect

    lsm/file_receive

    lsm/file_send_sigiot

Networking Hooks (Abused for lateral movement)

    lsm/socket_create

    lsm/socket_connect

    lsm/socket_listen

    lsm/socket_bind

    lsm/socket_accept

    lsm/socket_sendmsg

    lsm/socket_recvmsg

IPC & Shared Memory Hooks

    lsm/sem_alloc_security

    lsm/msg_queue_alloc_security

    lsm/shm_alloc_security

Miscellaneous Critical Hooks

    lsm/module_load → Block kernel module loading.

    lsm/kernfs_init_security

    lsm/ptrace_access_check

    lsm/ptrace_traceme

    lsm/mmap_file

    lsm/mmap_addr